{"format":1,"key":"zone:ironforge","path":"/lore/zone/ironforge","name":"Ironforge","kind":"zone","label":"Capital","zone":{"key":"ironforge","name":"Ironforge","path":"/lore/zone/ironforge"},"levels":"","description":"Carved into the heart of Ironforge Mountain in snowy Dun Morogh, Ironforge is the ancestral capital of the Bronzebeard dwarves and an unassailable…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:ironforge","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Carved into the heart of Ironforge Mountain in snowy Dun Morogh, Ironforge is the ancestral capital of the Bronzebeard dwarves and an unassailable bastion of the Alliance. Centered on the molten heat of the Great Forge, this sprawling underground city serves as a bustling hub of commerce, industry, and ancient dwarven lore. Under the steadfast rule of King Magni Bronzebeard, it now also shelters the displaced gnomes of nearby Gnomeregan.","Ironforge was founded twenty-five hundred years ago when the first generation of dwarves awakened in Uldaman and journeyed west into Dun Morogh's jagged peaks. Delving into the tallest mountain, they built a massive shrine to their titan progenitor Khaz'goroth alongside the colossal Great Forge. Ever since, the city has expanded in concentric rings around that fiery hearth. Unlike surface capitals, Ironforge is entirely enclosed beneath stone ceilings, warmed by roaring hearths and subterranean rivers of molten magma. Its fortified gates and cavernous depths have proven near-impregnable throughout centuries of war."],"hash":"48033d","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"84477f93a0","sec":67},"female-narrator":{"sha":"f0692e0611","sec":67}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Ironforge","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ironforge"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/magni-bronzebeard","n":"Magni Bronzebeard","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/great-forge","n":"Great Forge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tinker-town","n":"Tinker Town","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/de